Z||000014||terryk||12-18-2001||02:20 PM||||Exactly Ken (unless the agreement was something different.) Marriage is predefined as a male/female partnership in the western world and you agree to not mess around. If the agreement is otherwise (which is fine), don't call it marriage. Pick some other name. <P>I don't have a problem with alternate agreements, just don't redefine marriage to cover it. Pick another name and give the same rights if you want. While I'm not gay, I can appreciate the compassion between people.<P>There's no moral judgement here. I'm a poor judge of what makes people drag there a$$ out of bed everyday and face the world.<P>Part of being human is the ability to recognize when animal-procreation hardwiring is kicking in. I want to dork everything in sight, but I agreed not to. Infidelity is the instantaneous end of a marriage if either party wants it. Then when kids are involved, it really tests your soul....||||reg||1
Z||000015||JSocha||12-18-2001||02:37 PM||||Ray, sure the shoe would be on the other foot if it was a woman walking in on her husband, boy friend.<P>Swingers have basically come to a mutal consensus within their relationships and have gotten over their respective issues of jealousy.<P>Hardcore swingers, and to which some have had their marriages last 40+ years after shakier times in a monoagamouse relationship before turning to this have learned that just because they are married, their spouses are not their property.  Basically, its their body...not yours...not mine.<P>Marriage.  Yes individuals exchange vows.  Based on a long standing principle set fourth over many years of how we are "supposed" to act within these predefined, socially arranged, relationships. Governing rules.  However, are we meant to be monogamous?  I don't think so.  From the male standpoint, I'm with the belief, that we "will" seek out partners to pass our lineage on down the stream.  Women seek to find a mate that has strong attributes so her young will be strong.<P>Okay, my wife and I have been married only three years now.  Do I intend on cheating on her?  No...even though some of my posts may suggest that.  Its all in fun, but I am a little more liberal and open then my wife as she is very conservative and old fashioned in her beliefs.  Sometimes, I tease her that she is a Prude on certain issues where she is "OH NO!" and I'm like "AWSOME!".  <P>Even though I grew up under a governing principle of sexuality that was enforced by my parents, if they ever even talked about sex, as well as our church which preached that if you crossed pinkys while holding a song book while in church with a girl, you were having sex.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif">  Yes it was a Catholic Church.<P>To each his own.  What ever flips their boat.||||reg||1
Z||000016||JSocha||12-18-2001||02:42 PM||||BTW, marriage isn't a "religious" created institution as many of us have been taught and have been led to believe over time.<P>It was and is in fact a social-economical created institution which was created many, many moons and suns ago, before religion really formed and to which had nothing to do with religion at all.<P>Most religious philosophys later adopted it after the fact, creating a social and moral norm and that is what we have been taught up until today and into the future.<P>Jeff now dawns his flame suit for the retaliation that is now expected from bible thumpers.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
