Z||000031||JSocha||12-19-2001||12:37 AM||||Voytek, first of all, understandable, you don't know me.  I reveal a little of myself each time.<P>Second, I have a sarcastic and open-minded humor, to which my wife understands and I talk to her about these threads and she has the ability to come in here and see them anytime if she wishs as I have a shortcut directly to OT which she knows about and as this is the only place I really visit and post in, unless I need information someplace else.<P>About "being faithful".  Have had many opportunities to step out on my wife, even with some gals that my wife would even admit to being more attractive then her, to which I couldn't argue, yet I haven't, even when passes were made at me by and from them.  I am for the most parts liberal, but I can very well be conservative as well.<P>My wife knows I eye other women and I don't deny it when she catches or asks me.  If she asks what I think of them, I give her my honest opinion if either they are ugly or good looking and why I find them attractive.  I don't lie to her and I won't.  So I got a wondering eye.  What guy doesn't?  Does it mean I love my wife any less?  Absolutely not.<P>If my wife gets jealouse, which she does, but I do understand it was due to her last marriage and the mistrust she had there, I just let her know, and ask her why she is getting jealous as she has what they can not and will not have, and that is me.  But she knows I am not her property even though we tease each other about it.<P>Its jealousy and mistrust that eventually destroys a marriage or the proverbial your "my property".  Or better yet, the "Where were you?/Who were you talking too?" questions.<P>I've been married 3 years as well and was engaged several times before it finally happened and I did get married.  <P>Two times in which I had walked in on my fiancee's at the time, going at it.  Told them to leave the ring on the dresser, pack their things and be out no later then the next day.  I still talk with them.  And believe it or not, I harbored hard feelings towards them at first, but I harbor no hard feelings towards them now and in fact talk to them quiet frequently.  One is much happier which makes me happy knowing she wasn't stuck in a relationship she would later regret, the other one divorced and remarried several times now.  And because of it happening then, I am much happier now.  But I never cheated on them...again...even though I had many opportunties.<P>Yes, I said my wife is conservative and old fashioned to which she is.  Did I mean it negatively?  No.  Its those values in her that I admire the most and typically we as males seek in our partners so that hopefully we will keep our minds at peace so we won't come home to find them in bed with somebody else.<P>If I do, my "C-U! Wouldn't want to B-U!" comment would stand, because she would be the one giving up a lot if not everything, not me.  More then likely, I would be better off.<P>If I caught my wife with another women, it wouldn't bother me because its not a man that would be shagging my wife to which I would feel threatened, if that makes sense.<P>I myself as well as others don't need a "gospel" life in which to follow to be perfect.<P>I can be liberal and extremly open minded and yet conservative at the same time where need be.||||reg||1
Z||000032||Voytek||12-19-2001||10:36 AM||||Liberal and conservative are two opposites.  You can say you're both but you can't be both.<P>Having said that, I'm not saying that occasionally noticing another woman is wrong.  I'm guilty of that too and have been caught doing it (not persistently).  I'm sure my wife has noticed another guy here and there, too - she's probably more discrete about it, though.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">  This is human nature.  DESIRING someone else is a totally different thing, though.  Then we get into the 'what if you caught your spouse with someone else' scenario which started this topic.<P>You are right - too much jealousy CAN distroy a marriage / relationship, however, there IS a healthy dose of jealousy that absolutely needs to be present.  If it's not, then why would you care if you caught your wife with someone else?  (other than the marriage vows, of course).<P>All of us have 'opportunities'.  I've had more than I can count - it kinda feels nice  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/redface.gif">: .  <P>At this point I am uncertain where this discussion is going.  I agree with you on some points, disagree on others.  Let's leave it at that.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P><B>No one is worth shooting over. None.</B><P>Good point, terryk, unless (like someone said) you're protecting your family.||||reg||1
Z||000033||JSocha||12-19-2001||10:49 AM||||Actually one can be both liberal and/or conservative depending on the situtaion.  Can't have one with out the other.  Just like there are two sides to a coin.  You can view and present either side.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>BTW Voytek, I wasn't upset with you in my last post, just extremly tired as I had just gotten back from Minot with the wife and daughter as they finally finished up their Christmas Shopping.<P>We are all learning about each other here on the forum.  As I said, understandable, you don't know me and I don't know you.  And of course I, as well as others reveal a little more about themselves each time they post.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Do I practice Swinging?  No.  Would I like to?  Arguable.  &lt;sigh&gt;  What guy hasn't wondered and/or fantasized about it at one time or another, to enjoy and/or taste some fruits from the other dish of dessert?!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> hehehe  I'm only human...and of course a male full of active hormones.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||6
